# Game Theory, People Power and Philippine Politics.

**Authors:** Lee-Chua, Queena N.

## Abstract
Delineates two illustrative game-theoretic applications to Philippine politics: (1) People Power Revolution in the mid-1980s and (2) conflict over Spratly Islands in the mid-1990s. Uses zero-sum games to model these two events, and elementary matrix theory to determine pure strategies and locate equilibrium points. Includes recommendations for using game theory in other political situations in an attempt to bridge the gap between the classroom and the real world. (Author/ASK)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ618764

